/* analog-canvas-extensions 0.4: 0.3, and six more definitions of meaning only (since 0.4): the
   typography of a drawing text, the parameters of a part that the netlist does not print, a part
   that has no name, the variant a part is drawn as, the name of a Cell, and the top Cell.
   0.3: 0.2, whose $CANVAS_TYPESETTING also gives how wires that cross without connecting are drawn
   (crossings, since 0.3).
   0.2: 0.1, and four definitions of meaning only (below, since 0.2).
   Generated by build-std.mjs in rnl-dev (notes/analog-canvas-rnl-import-export/std-0.3, eb3a4ce)
   from Analog Canvas 5008996af (packages/components/definitions), symbol-list.json (rnl-dev 693cc69)
   and the hand-written parts there; from here on edited in rnl, whose files are the source.
   Not standard: Analog Canvas's appearance variants of standard symbols, named $CANVAS_ and its
   component id, and its chopper; and, since 0.2, facts of its drawings that the netlist does not
   keep. A file names it with USE-PACKAGE (16.2); the core does not bundle it.
   Written in the language 0.3, as the standard series 0.3 is.
   Coordinates are y-up; one unit is one grid step, ten Analog Canvas units. Pins bind by terminal
   number, so a symbol fits any dialect. */
@RNL(type="header") { @VERSION("0.3"); @PACKAGE(name="analog-canvas-extensions", version="0.4")}

